# .git deliberately SHIPS in the build context: the Dockerfile build stage
# derives VERSION/COMMIT from `git describe` (see the RUN in Dockerfile /
# Dockerfile.builder). It is never COPYed into a runtime image, only read by
# the build stage — the cost is context transfer size (~42MB) on remote
# daemons. Pass explicit --build-arg VERSION/COMMIT in CI to pin or avoid it.
bin/
dist/
data/
*.db
*.log
.env
docs/
scripts/
.github/

# deploy/: keep ONLY the sidecar build materials (the nfsd/samba Dockerfiles
# and the entrypoints they COPY — compose builds them from this context).
# Excluded via children-wildcard (not `deploy/`) so the ! negations work:
# a file under an excluded directory cannot be re-included.
deploy/*
!deploy/Dockerfile.nfsd
!deploy/Dockerfile.samba
!deploy/nfsd
!deploy/samba
